  "chapter": {
    "number": 83,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(84) For the end, a Psalm for the sons of Core, concerning the wine presses."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "How amiable are your tabernacles, O Lord of hosts!",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My soul longs, and faints for the courts of the Lord: my heart and my flesh have exulted in the living god.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yes, the sparrow has found himself a home, and the turtle-dove a nest for herself, where she may lay her young, even your altars, O Lord of hosts, my King, and my God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed are they that dwell in your house: they will praise you evermore. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed is the man whose help is of you, O Lord; in his heart he has purposed to go up",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "the valley of weeping, to the place which he has appointed, for there the law-giver will grant blessings.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall go from strength to strength: the God of gods shall be seen in Sion.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord God of hosts, hear my prayer: listen, O God of Jacob. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Behold, O God our defender, and look upon the face of your anointed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For one day in your courts is better than thousands. I would rather be an abject in the house of God, than dwell in the tents of sinners.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the Lord loves mercy and truth: God will give grace and glory: the Lord will not withhold good things from them that walk in innocence.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord of hosts, blessed is the man that trusts in you.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
